lines and recommendations for nutritional practices in surgical weight loss patients.", "ASMBS:The American Society for Metabolic and Bariatric Surgery (ASMBS) is an organization that focuses on the treatment of obesity and related conditions through surgical methods.", "LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY:Laparoscopic surgery is a minimally invasive surgical technique that uses small incisions and specialized instruments, often resulting in quicker recovery times.", "VERY LOW CALORIE DIET (VLCD):VLCD is a dietary regimen that provides very low caloric intake, often used in conjunction with bariatric surgery to promote weight loss.", "POSTOPERATIVE CARE:Postoperative care involves the management and monitoring of patients after surgery to ensure proper recovery and address any complications.", "DIEETARY MANAGEMENT:Dietary management refers to the planning and implementation of a diet tailored to meet the specific needs of patients, especially after surgical procedures.", "DIETARY MANAGEMENT:Dietary management involves adjusting food intake to effectively manage symptoms associated with metabolic disorders, including conditions such as galactosaemia and lactose intolerance. This approach focuses on tailoring dietary choices to alleviate the impact of these disorders on an individual's health and well-being.", "POSE:POSE (Primary Obesity Surgery Endolumenal) is a procedure suggested for treating obesity before considering bariatric surgery.", "BALÓN INTRAGÁSTRICO:The intragastric balloon (BIG) is a temporary therapeutic strategy for significant weight loss before bariatric surgery.", "GASTRECTOMÍA ENDOSCÓPICA (APOLLO):The endoscopic vertical gastrectomy (Apollo) aims to mimic surgical gastrectomy by suturing the stomach internally.", "ENDOBARRIER:EndoBarrier is a medical device designed for the treatment of obesity and type 2 diabetes, primarily by regulating gastrointestinal hormones. This innovative device, also known as the endoluminal bypass or endobarrier, is strategically placed in the duodenum to inhibit food absorption, thereby enhancing glycemic control in individuals with diabetes. Through its mechanism of action, EndoBarrier aims to provide a non-surgical option for managing these conditions effectively.", "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2 (DM2):Type 2 diabetes (DM2) is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and can be improved through weight loss.", "NUTRICIÓN Y SOPORTE METABÓLICO:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}